//empty class have sizeof(object) = 1 
#include <iostream>
using namespace std;

class A {};

int main()
{
    A obj1;
    A obj2;

    cout << sizeof(obj1) << endl;

    cout << &obj1 << endl;
    cout << &obj2 << endl;
}

output
1
0x61ff08
0x61ff07

The compiler gives at least 1 byte so that different objects can have unique memory addresses.

Empty class ka object bhi memory mein exist karta hai, isliye C++ uska size 0 nahi rakhta; generally minimum 1 byte rakha jata hai, taaki different objects ko distinct addresses diye ja saken.
